# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.9 — THE TRASH ROW STOPS CARRYING WHO DELETED IT
# `Reads.trash/2` reads the governance trail (`aud_event.record_archived`) for each trashed page and
# puts its `aud_actor_id` on the row as `deleted_by` (from which the surface derives "you" / the
# member's name / "a workspace member"). Dropping the projection leaves the row with no deleter at
# all, so the view renders WHEN and silently omits WHO — the exact regression a "who deleted this?"
# affordance exists to prevent. The trash still lists, still restores, and every other assertion in
# the suite stays green.
#
# Aimed at the ROW projection only: the audit read, the scope attribution, the name resolution, the
# restore path and the label rules are untouched.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a workspace-scope deletion reads as 'a workspace member'
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/reads.ex
@@ -465,8 +465,7 @@
   defp project_trashed(doc, deleted_by, deleted_by_name) do
     doc
     |> project_doc()
     |> Map.put(:archived_at, Map.get(doc, :archived_at))
-    |> Map.put(:deleted_by, deleted_by)
     |> Map.put(:deleted_by_name, deleted_by_name)
   end
 
